A||N||5||Bob Englert||Rear Trunk Gasket||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||02-08-2001||09:31 PM||||I need to replace the rear trunk gasket in my 87 GT.  I am having a serious water leak problem and the gasket is torn badly.<P>1) How is the gasket secured to the trunk edge?<P>2) Where should I look to see if I need to seal the trunk edges before installing the gasket?  <P>Thanks...<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||02-09-2001||02:55 AM||||Bob, the gasket is sealed around it with silicon (or, if you are desparate you can use RTV!) - it just fits on a metal ridge all the way around. There are drain holes at each rear corner under the gasket which should remain free of sealant (you'll see what I mean when you peel the old gasket off - there is a water channel there........truthfully, I installed a new one about a year ago on my '87GT and have yet to seal it - still doesn't leak tho!||||reg||1
Z||000002||jasonl||02-09-2001||08:48 AM||||I have one that is also torn.  Is that something you have to get at the dealer, or does someone like the Fiero Factory have this?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||02-09-2001||08:55 AM||||Fiero Store has it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-09-2001||02:56 PM||||Are you sure the water is coming in via the torn seal?  My 85GT leaks water into the trunk through the luggage rack mounts. I will replace the grommets.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||02-09-2001||03:48 PM||||I ordered a replacement gasket from GMPartsDirect.com<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
